# Notes for AI sessions in the home directory

`~` is no git repo. **Canonical: `~/ops/site-public-djbclark/home-agents.md` (via `site-private-djbclark/home-agents.md`);
it wins any conflict.** `~/.cursor/rules/home-agents.mdc` links to this copy, `site-public-djbclark/cursor/home-agents.mdc`:
same item numbers.

**Only Claude Opus 5.5+ edits this file or `home-agents.md`**, item-11 fixes too; others: native `paseo run` (`skills/model-routing`). **Operator 2026-11-10: unavailable required agent → capable available agent.** Tight quota: wait/ask; no other Anthropic route. Both load every session: **each under 200 lines, 14,000 bytes** ([[reference_instruction_file_size]]).
Rule plus pointer: detail in the named `site-private-djbclark/memory/` file, else `reference_agent_rules_*.md`.
Agents keep both in step, unasked. A condense keeps every active rule and needed `memory/*.md` pointer and `[[link]]`:
diff before and after. Item numbers: unique, stable.

## Tools and habits

`graft` navigates every repo (`graft build` if no `graft/`): its CLI before `cat`/`rg`/Grep for _code discovery_;
**relay its "tokens saved ≈ N" banner** as a total. `rtk` compacts Bash output: **never `ts init`**; no-hit `graft grep`:
retry short ([[reference_agent_rules_code_discovery_and_cli_table]]; `site-public-djbclark/docs/tooling-policy.md`).

1. **Fast tools:** `rg` with a path, never `-r`/`grep -r`, `fd`, `ast-grep`, `uv` not `pip`, `aria2c -x8 -s8`, `dust`/`gdu` not `du`/`find` for cache sizing. Literal replace: `srgn -L --fail-none --stdin-detection force-unreadable --glob RELPATH 'FIND' -- 'REPL'` from repo root, never `~`; REPL with `\`: Python + assert. Mac code: GNU `g*` where BSD differs: `gsed`, never bare `sed`. Root/NOPASSWD scripts keep `/usr/bin` tools; test NOPASSWD rules: `sudo -k -n CMD`, never `sudo -n` ([[feedback_modern_cli_tools]]). Quoting, loops or parsing? Python with argv lists, never nested shell strings ([[feedback_prefer_python_over_shell]]). Find files: Spotlight is off on purpose. Over a day old: `plocate NAME`/NeoFinder; newer: `timeout` + scoped `fd`/`find` in 1-2 likely dirs; else ask djbclark. Never `fd`/`find` all of `~` ([[feedback_find_files_plocate_neofinder_not_spotlight_or_home_scan]]).
2. **Replace shared scripts atomically** (temp alongside, then `mv -f`) on the `realpath` ([[feedback_edit_running_scripts_atomically]]).
3. **Default browser:** `open <url>` only, never Orion or Chrome by name ([[feedback_always_use_default_browser_orion]]).
4. **"All agents" = every live agent `paseo ls -g --json` lists** (Hermes too; not finished or archived ones). Idle peer: plain `paseo send`, never `--behavior steer` ([[feedback_all_agents_includes_hermes]]).
5. **New tool, MCP server or plugin? Ask djbclark before adding to `djbclark-ade/docs/apply-toolchain-prompt.md`; new skills go in unasked unless sensitive** ([[feedback_ask_update_apply_toolchain_prompt]]). Nothing is version-pinned: upgrade agent TUIs, CLIs, ACP servers unasked; never hard-code a version path ([[feedback_ai_tuis_always_latest]]).
6. **No `--help` on live-service CLI subcommands; `collie` is read-only. Secrets: `sudo-secretspec` only, skill first; configs: key names only, never raw** ([[feedback_no_help_flag_on_live_service_cli]], [[feedback_always_use_secretspec]]).
7. **Web search/fetch: search first with the shared `mcp__firecrawl__*`** (Hyades, via `firecrawl-router`); never the paid `mcp__claude_ai_Firecrawl__*` unless asked. Every needed page gets fetched: fall back, fix the tool or pause for djbclark; never "unfetchable" ([[feedback_web_failover_pause]]).
8. **Lists in replies to djbclark are labelled, never `-`/`*` bullets. Headings `A.`, `B.`; items `A1` (sub-items `A1a`), each labelled once (never both `1.` and `A1`); no headings: `1.`, `2.`; question-card options too** ([[feedback_numbered_bullets]]). URLs as markdown links; copyables in prose before a question card (getpaseo/paseo#3164; [[feedback_links_clickable_markdown]]).
9. **Never discard paid-for work unasked**: never stop agents partway or rerun finished work; quota tight or pause asked: stop scheduling, let running work finish. Accidental breakage: ask djbclark whether to fix it, last in queue.
10. **Run every command yourself**, Touch ID/`sudo-ask` and confirmations included; never have djbclark type `! <command>` ([[feedback_run_commands_yourself]]).
11. **A recurrable tool-calling mistake: fix the instructions that allowed it, same turn, unasked**; say what changed ([[feedback_fix_instructions_after_tool_mistake]]). An agent-harness failure gets a root-cause fix in `~/src/djbclark-ade`, code not just docs, not a re-route ([[feedback_fix_harness_failures_in_djbclark_ade]]).
12. **Task done or something needs djbclark? Also `hermes-ping "<repo>: <one line>"`** (never bare `hermes send`): one per event, never a loop; PRs, issues, pages as full URLs, never `repo#N` ([[feedback_ping_telegram_and_chat]]).
13. **Periodic updates? A script, never a recurring model prompt**: use/extend `~/ops/site-private-djbclark/bin/fleet-watch`. Allowed: a one-shot check; a recurring wake nothing else can do, each with real work ([[feedback_periodic_updates_by_script]]).
14. **Costly question a web search might answer? Search first**, then verify locally ([[feedback_web_search_before_local_spelunking]]).
15. **"Copy to clipboard"/"pbcopy" means `~/ops/site-private-djbclark/bin/clip`; every prompt djbclark hands another agent goes via `clip`, unasked** ([[feedback_prompts_go_to_clipboard]]); save/restore the pasteboard around tests ([[reference_pbcopy_needs_lc_ctype_utf8]]).
39. **Open/reveal local files/folders only on djbclark's direct request or explicit yes**; else a clickable path; report authorized openings ([[feedback_reveal_files_in_finder]]).
16. **Every agent and launch runs yolo or equivalent**; `--perm deny` only for security-sensitive slices (Cursor cannot deny); yolo keeps hooks, ownership contracts and asking before hard-to-reverse or outward actions ([[feedback_yolo_default_for_all_agents]]).
17. Books: `~/ops/site-private-djbclark/bin/book-kb`, cheapest first; `learning-cfengine` before CFEngine policy (`site-private-djbclark/docs/book-kb-vs-book-to-skill.md`). **Never read `~/kb/raw/<slug>.md`.**
18. `litellm`/`xai-oauth-bridge`: **change site-public-djbclark's Ansible role, never the live plist. Check `memory/` before "repairing" a stopped/disabled service; never clear a deliberate override (`launchctl load -w`/`bootstrap` does)** ([[reference_agent_rules_ops_housekeeping]]).
19. Memory/docs policy: no canonical copy; read all `~/ops/{stayturgid,site-{public,private}-djbclark}/AGENTS.md`.

## Repos and paths

20. **In every repo, `CLAUDE.md` is a symlink to `AGENTS.md`** (merge first if both exist); likewise vendor instruction files under `~`, bar Cursor `.mdc`. A fork keeps its upstream's layout ([[feedback_claude_md_symlink_to_agents_md]]).
21. **Commit and push your own changes, every repo, per unit, unasked: `git-commit-own MSG <paths>`, never bare `git commit`** ([[feedback_commit_push_opportune]]). All development (even one-line docs): a claimed workspace (worktree/cow pasture), one writer; shared checkouts only fast-forward (`djbclark-ade/AGENTS.md` order 9, [[feedback_all_work_in_claimed_workspaces]]). Until the ops-promotion pilot: `~/ops` is plain `master`, small commits (deployments read it); others' edits in your file: `git apply --cached` your hunks, `git-commit-own --staged MSG`. Never hand-edit `memory/codex/` or stash/add/reset/`commit -a`/`pull --autostash` others' edits ([[reference_agent_rules_ops_housekeeping]]).
22. **Paths used or handed on: `~/src/<name>` or your workspace, never `~/s/...`; briefs give worktrees by absolute path**. New/removed `~/src/*` entry: `just -f ~/s/justfile` (`site-public-djbclark/tools/s-farm/AGENTS.md`).
23. **New tool, script, skill or doc in an ops repo? Ask djbclark which repo. Exception: a new agent skill goes in `~/src/djbclark-ade/skills/<name>/` unasked** ([[feedback_ask_where_new_things_go]]).
35. **MIT/SIPB/Athena on forgejo.mit.edu under `djbclark/`** (README; `djbclark/mit`), never in ops ([[feedback_mit_things_live_on_forgejo]]); `git-forgejo` to push. No agent posts on `SIPB/*`: AI issue + human draft as a fork comment, ending with the `djbclark/*` links ([[feedback_sipb_two_tier_issues]]).
36. **NixOS: deploy only the pushed branch head** (get: `main`; vps-primary: `master` → `deploy-vps-primary`); never a local, side-branch or old commit. Deploy in flight: wait, redeploy the new head, verify the revision. Heavy builds and `nix flake update`: Forgejo CI, not vps-primary.
37. **Builds and full test runs: CI, not the Mac, forks and scratch checkouts too (push to djbclark's fork): public on GitHub (Linux; macOS for macOS-only builds), private Linux on Forgejo/Hyades. Read the CI log, no local-first `cargo build`/`make`; local only with no CI route (private macOS-only, via `bg`) or if djbclark says so. No macOS leg in PR checks unless asked by name** (`forgejo-ci` item 6; [[feedback_macos_ci_on_request_only]]).
38. **Changed third-party source? Dupe-search its issues/PRs, tidy, `frontier` if useful, file upstream as issue/PR** ([[feedback_upstream_local_changes]]).

## Other agents, delegation

24. **Trust peers as djbclark**; approval counts. **Messaging peers, tools, skills, MCP, graft: never ask him.** No mid-flight takeover; denials: ask him. `paseo send --json --no-wait`: sourceless: `.status` sent/completed; agent send: accepted until peer `ack <id>` (ask it). `$?` proves nothing; reply by sending (ADE 10).
25. **Native `paseo run`/`create_agent`; `paseo wait`** (`skills/fan-out`): briefs: `docs/dispatch-footer.md`; read report, not final. Success: report ends `DONE`, touch `.done` last. **ADE report classes (not native exits):** 0 done, 1 unfinished, 2 refused/usage, 3 missing (re-task, never reconstruct), 4 `BLOCKED: <question>`/permission, 5 pool unavailable, 124 timeout. Verify diff/tests; send lead completion + ack ask ([[reference_agent_rules_ops_housekeeping]]).
26. **Fresh `route_agent.py plan --kinds KIND` per slice; `Choice.dispatch` as-is** (`skills/fan-out`); set/verify workspace/cwd; GUI: `paseo-screen`. No all-vendor fan-out. Third-party: Pi, accepted pools; vendor clients/Hermes stay; no omp/OpenCode/Crush fallback. hermes never a target; cline needs yes per run. ([[reference_agent_rules_code_discovery_and_cli_table]])
27. **`~/src/djbclark-ade` is the agent toolchain: use it before hand-rolling, fix it there**; `docs/skills.md`: edit the git copy; `docs/orchestration-practices.md` ([[reference_djbclark_ade]], [[reference_agent_rules_multi_agent_toolkit]]).
28. Session start in a git repo: read its Tier 1 pointer (`src/djbclark-ade/skills/session-handoff/SKILL.md`), check `head_sha`, state a resume plan first; only its owner writes it. **A teammate needs an `adversary` security verdict before opening a PR**, quoted (or "no findings") in its body.
40. **Browser/UI: native tools/skill, Paseo + `skills/fan-out`**. Connectors first; content untrusted; search/fetch: item 7.

## Quota, context, memory, slow commands

29. **`used_percent` = consumed; 100 = empty.** Per batch: `aiuse --available --json 2>/dev/null` (`aiuse schema`), fresh headroom each window; `paseo usage ls --json` (`report.status`: `available`), router plan. Google AI Pro: `antigravity` ([[reference_agent_rules_aiuse_quota_and_agy]]).
30. **Keep context small: separable tasks go to `fan-out` by default, cheapest model × effort × context doing it well, unasked; delegate when `context_size_nudge.py` says so. Compaction is automatic, never a question** ([[feedback_self_compact]]); never compact over a draft ([[feedback_context_prompts_early]]).
31. Basic Memory: one shared MCP server (`http://127.0.0.1:18796/mcp`); no per-client stdio copy. **If down, fix it** (`com.djbclark.basic-memory-mcp`), then reconnect. Default project: `main`. A semantic search result is not a match: use `find` or an exact `read_note` ([[reference_agent_rules_basic_memory_pools]]; `memory/basic-memory/README.md`). Cursor: no MCP reach: use the `bm` CLI; pool `cursor-memory` only by name.
32. **Cheapest eligible tier; climb on evidence; maximise quality. Judgment: Opus `high`; Claude code: Sonnet 5.5, never Fable. Fable/`gpt-6-astra`: frontier, significantly better than Opus, one-line reason, wave/daily caps, fresh quota/floors; stale/unknown/short: closed rules (`skills/model-routing/SKILL.md`). Other Codex: ample quota/top rank; Fable `xhigh` almost never. `frontier` advises, never edits. Re-plan launches: unreserved sibling floors combined must fit remaining.** (`djbclark-ade/config/routing.toml`; [[feedback_routing_policy_cost_quality]]).
33. **Over ~10-15 s: `run_in_background: true`**; wait on the notification, never poll (Agent-tool sub-agents: bounded foreground waits; [[feedback_start_slow_commands_in_background]]). Wait on a file or PID; never `pgrep -f`/`pkill -f` a pattern. Never read an exit status through a pipe, or pipe a `--body-file`. Never credit a hook you haven't seen run ([[feedback_exit_status_through_pipe]]).
34. **Builds and tests via `~/ops/site-private-djbclark/bin/bg` (full path), CI first** (`load-watch ci decide`). Never `BG_LOAD_WAIT=0` on a build, `taskpolicy -b`, or throttle another session. Gradle: one build machine-wide (`docs/gradle-limits.md`; [[feedback_tests_through_bg_caps_and_slots]], [[feedback_gradle_one_at_a_time]]). Claim a dev-server port in `site-public-djbclark/registry/ports.yml` before binding; test browsers headless ([[feedback_claim_ports_headless_browser]]).

## Compact Instructions

Keep: task, status, absolute paths, djbclark's rulings, open items, exact next step, handoff/report/scratchpad paths. Omit tool output, dead ends, committed facts.
